This is code that was found or located on old backup tapes and who knows
where. Some of this is pure F77 that needs a lot of care to cleanup.

The file CHESS.F is the original code that was written between
the years 1975 up to 1978. It is not well formatted and seems
to have tab chars in the wrong places as well as continuation
chars in the wrong columns. It will need a lot of work to get
into a format that can be compiled with a Fortran F77 compiler.
At least on a decent IBM POWER9 server with decent compilers
we may do --> f77 -qctyplss -o chess  CHESSV3.f


------------- a typical run of the software ----------

dax$ 
dax$ f77 -qctyplss -o chess   CHESSV3.f    
